   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py:22` prints `note['created']` as-is. It does no date formatting of its own.\n- `fieldnotes/store.py:25` creates that value with `datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()`. That gives strings like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`, which is ISO-8601 with a UTC offset.\n- I searched the Python files for `strftime` and `toLocale`. There are no locale-style formats anywhere in the code.\n\n`list` prints whatever string is stored in `notes.json`. If an older or hand-edited file holds a non-ISO `created` value, `list` would print it unchanged. Nothing in the code produces such a value. I didn't check any existing `notes.json`, and I didn't look at `tools/check.py`.\n\nI made no changes.",
