   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`. It prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`, for example `2026-01-02: first`. The project checks pass: both unit tests ran OK and no line is over 100 characters.\n\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the date part of the stored timestamp (`YYYY-MM-DD`), not the full ISO time. If you want the full timestamp, change `created[:10]` to `created` in `fieldnotes/cli.py`.\n- **Usage text:** I moved the usage string into one `USAGE` constant and added `export` to it.\n- **Test:** the new test is in `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes, runs `export`, and checks the output lines.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` requires `NOTES_HOME`, so I ran it with that set to a fresh temp directory and didn't touch any real notes.",
